What is GitHub Actions?

GitHub Actions is a continuous integration and continuous deployment (CI/CD) service built into GitHub. 
It lets you automate software development workflows whenever certain events occur in your repository.

Where can you find GitHub Actions?

You can find GitHub Actions in the Actions tab of a GitHub repository.

Steps to access GitHub Actions
Open your repository on GitHub.
At the top of the repository page, click the Actions tab.
Here you can:
View workflow runs.
Create a new workflow.
Monitor build and deployment status.
Re-run failed workflows.
View workflow logs.

If your repository doesn't have any workflows yet,
GitHub will suggest starter workflow templates based on your project's language or framework.

